---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Post.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../../../siteconfig';
export const title = `${SITE_TITLE} 4.0`;
export const description = `One set of conventions across every component, real form validation, overlays in the top layer, and more than 50 new components for enterprise apps.`;
export const publishedDate = '2026-11-07';
export const tags = ['release'];
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} publishedDate={publishedDate} tags={tags}>
  <p>
    {SITE_TITLE} 4.0 is the biggest release so far. Every component now follows the same conventions, so once you
    know one you know them all, and the library grows from about 80 to more than 120 components. Upgrading from 3.x?
    The <a class='link' href='https://github.com/redvars/peacock/blob/main/MIGRATION.md'>migration guide</a> lists
    every change.
  </p>

  <h2 class='text-headline-small'>One way to do things</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Events.</strong> Every field fires <code class='text-code-block'>input</code> and
      <code class='text-code-block'>change</code> with <code class='text-code-block'>detail.value</code>; every overlay
      fires <code class='text-code-block'>open</code> and <code class='text-code-block'>close</code> with a
      <code class='text-code-block'>reason</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Words.</strong> <code class='text-code-block'>intent</code> for meaning,
      <code class='text-code-block'>variant</code> for style, <code class='text-code-block'>current</code> for the page
      you are on, <code class='text-code-block'>start</code> and <code class='text-code-block'>end</code> for sides that
      follow the writing direction.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sizes.</strong> One scale, <code class='text-code-block'>xs</code> to <code class='text-code-block'>xl</code>,
      with fields and buttons at the same height by default.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class='text-headline-small'>Foundations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Forms.</strong> Fields take part in native validation, block submission while invalid and show the message under the field. <code class='text-code-block'>wc-form</code> adds an error summary, unsaved-changes tracking and server errors.</li>
    <li><strong>Overlays.</strong> Modals, sheets, menus, popovers, tooltips and toasts render in the top layer, stack correctly, trap and return focus, and close with Escape one at a time.</li>
    <li><strong>Everywhere.</strong> Translatable text with <code class='text-code-block'>setPeacockStrings()</code>, right-to-left layouts, a density setting and high-contrast support.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class='text-headline-small'>New components</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Data:</strong> a data grid with column resize, reorder, groups, multi-sort, row details, inline editing, grouping, totals, virtual scrolling and CSV export; a filter bar, description list, stat, sparkline, virtual list, kanban, JSON viewer and diff viewer.</li>
    <li><strong>Inputs:</strong> password with rules, PIN, phone, currency, date range, mention, inline edit, rating, signature, file upload, checkbox group, listbox, transfer list and tree.</li>
    <li><strong>App:</strong> app shell, page header, stack, grid, resizable panels, scroll area, stepper, anchor navigation, command palette, workspace switcher, user menu, notification center, banner, confirm dialog, hover card, tour and comment thread; illustrations for empty, error and success screens, and the Redvars loader.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class='text-headline-small'>Removed</h2>
  <p>
    Everything deprecated during 3.x is gone, including <code class='text-code-block'>wc-notification</code>
    (use <code class='text-code-block'>wc-alert</code> or <code class='text-code-block'>wc-snackbar</code>),
    <code class='text-code-block'>wc-sidebar-menu</code> (use <code class='text-code-block'>wc-navigation-drawer</code>),
    <code class='text-code-block'>wc-spinner</code> (use <code class='text-code-block'>wc-circular-progress</code>)
    and <code class='text-code-block'>wc-empty-state</code> (compose your own message from <code class='text-code-block'>wc-illustration</code>, a heading, text and buttons).
  </p>
</Layout>
